        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe structural decision is right: this is an owner\u2192DTO derived field, and the file already establishes exactly this pattern (`toDisplayName`, `toInitials`, `toMembershipTier` as `default` helpers wired via `@Mapping(expression=...)`). `toLocality` slots in cleanly, isn't duplicated anywhere, and the mapper is the natural home for it. One idiomatic nit only:\n\n- **Fully-qualified `java.util.Map` instead of an import** (`OwnerMapper.java:28`). The file already imports its other `java.util` types (`Collection` at line 12, `List` at line 13). Using inline FQNs for `java.util.Map` and `java.util.Map.of(...)` breaks the file's own convention and reads awkwardly. Add `import java.util.Map;` and write `Map<String, String> CITY_REGION = Map.of(...)` to match the surrounding style.\n\nEverything else \u2014 the constant placement, the `getOrDefault(..., \"UNKNOWN\")` derivation, the doc comments, and the mirrored OpenAPI schema entry \u2014 is coherent and additive."
